# Line-ending policy for a cross-platform repo deployed to Linux containers.
#
# `* text=auto` stores text files with LF in the repository. The explicit rules
# below force LF in the WORKING COPY too for files that must never carry CRLF:
#   • docker-entrypoint.sh — a CRLF shebang (#!/bin/sh\r) makes the Linux
#     container fail with "bad interpreter" after a Windows checkout.
#   • *.sql (Prisma migrations) — keep byte-stable for `migrate deploy`.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never touch line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
